 "script": "Turkey's in, guests are coming. Wait. Why is the oven cold?\n\nNo problem. Homie's got a hair dryer!\n\nThree hours later. The turkey is still raw. My hair is not.\n\nHere's the thing. An electric range lasts about thirteen years. A gas range, about fifteen.\n\nSo when yours quits before the big day, do this.\n\nOne. Check the easy stuff: the clock is set, the door lock is off, and it's plugged in.\n\nTwo. Find your manufacturer or home warranty, and read what's covered and the service fee.\n\nThree. Book the repair before the holiday rush, and get the repair or replace quote in writing.\n\nIf Homie can figure it out, so can you.",
